# UI (Inventory Dashboard)

## Purpose

Visual and interaction consistency for the dealership inventory screen. Backend adapts to this UI; pages are not redesigned to match API shapes.

## When it applies

Any UI markup, styling, dialogs, badges, layouts, or new screens under `frontend/src`.

## Required practices

### Source of truth

- Shared components under `frontend/src/components/` (once scaffolded).
- Patterns: inventory list with filters (make, model, aging), clear distinction between normal stock and aging stock, proposed-action control on aging rows.
- Copy uses glossary terms — not “status”, “aged unit”, “brand”.

### Page composition

- List: filters + table/cards; aging rows visually distinct (badge/tone already used on the page).
- Primary image: `<img src={apiImageUrl}>` or equivalent same-origin route; placeholder when `has_primary_image` is false.
- Forms/dialogs: smallest control set — stock-out, set proposed action, upload/replace/remove image as separate actions.
- Feedback: inline field errors + toast on success/failure.

### Change bar

Only change UI when:

1. Backend cannot express the feature, or
2. Product explicitly requires a new field/control.

Then: smallest diff, same spacing/typography/components.

## Must never do

- Drive-by restyle unrelated pages while implementing a filter or action.
- Invent a second navigation shell for the same dashboard.
- Show MinIO or internal object keys to the manager.
- Use emoji-heavy or marketing-hero layouts inconsistent with an ops dashboard.

